{"name":"China Aster","hex":"#444c60","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"china","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of porcelain, a hard white translucent ceramic made from kaolin, now  sometimes distinguished in reference to tableware as fine or good china.","Chinaware: porcelain tableware."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/china"},{"term":"aster","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several plants of the genus Aster; one of its flowers.","A star-shaped structure formed during the mitosis of a cell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aster"}],"entries":[{"title":"Callistephus","blocks":[{"text":"Callistephus is a monotypic genus of flowering plants in the aster family, Asteraceae, containing the single species Callistephus chinensis. Its common names include China aster and annual aster. It is native to China and Korea. and it is cultivated worldwide as an ornamental plant in cottage gardens and as a cut flower."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Asterales_-_Callistephus_chinensis_-_20120823.jpg/330px-Asterales_-_Callistephus_chinensis_-_20120823.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Callistephus"},{"title":"Aster (genus)","blocks":[{"text":"Aster is a genus of perennial flowering plants in the family Asteraceae. Its circumscription has been narrowed, and it now encompasses around 170 species, all but one of which are restricted to Eurasia; many species formerly in Aster are now in other genera of the tribe Astereae. Aster amellus is the type species of the genus and the family Asteraceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Asteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG/330px-Asteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aster_(genus)"},{"title":"China","blocks":[{"text":"China, officially the People's Republic of China (PRC), is a country in East Asia. It is divided into 33 province-level divisions, including two special administrative regions. Beijing is the capital, while Shanghai is the most populous city by urban area. Its geography features the Central Plain, major rivers such as the Yangtze and Yellow River, deserts, subtropical and temperate forests, plateaus, and mountain ranges such as the Himalayas. It is the world's second-most populous country after India, with a population exceeding 1.4 billion. Covering 9.6 million square kilometers (3,700,000 sq mi), it is the third largest country by area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/%EA%B3%BC%EA%BD%83_%EA%B0%80%EA%B9%8C%EC%9D%B4.JPG/120px-%EA%B3%BC%EA%BD%83_%EA%B0%80%EA%B9%8C%EC%9D%B4.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/%EA%B3%BC%EA%BD%83_%EA%B0%80%EA%B9%8C%EC%9D%B4.JPG/250px-%EA%B3%BC%EA%BD%83_%EA%B0%80%EA%B9%8C%EC%9D%B4.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/%EA%B3%BC%EA%BD%83_%EA%B0%80%EA%B9%8C%EC%9D%B4.JPG/120px-%EA%B3%BC%EA%BD%83_%EA%B0%80%EA%B9%8C%EC%9D%B4.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%EA%B3%BC%EA%BD%83_%EA%B0%80%EA%B9%8C%EC%9D%B4.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/China_Aster_%28Callistephus_Chinensis%29.jpg/120px-China_Aster_%28Callistephus_Chinensis%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut